cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CrashDefNet, please cite it as below."
title: "CrashDefNet: Graph Neural Network Surrogates for Crash Simulation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stocker
    given-names: Felix
    email: felix.stocker@sto-eng.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23575635
repository-code: "https://github.com/stofe94/crash-def-net"
abstract: >-
  CrashDefNet is a complete, lean PyTorch research framework for graph neural
  network surrogates of crash simulation. It learns from finite element runs and
  predicts autoregressively, step by step on the mesh, how a structure deforms. It
  covers the chain from raw simulation data to evaluation against published results
  and implements MeshGraphNets and the MeshGraphNet-Transformer (MGN-T) in one
  pipeline, evaluated with the metrics of the MGN-T paper on DeepMind's
  deforming_plate benchmark and on OpenRadioss runs of a bumper beam against a pole.
keywords:
  - graph neural networks
  - autoregressive prediction
  - MeshGraphNets
  - MeshGraphNet-Transformer
  - crash simulation
  - CAE
  - finite element method
  - surrogate model
